[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2888348948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106518#issuecomment-2888348948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106518","id":2888348948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sKLUU","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-17T12:18:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-17T12:29:14Z","body":"~~I can see how this is misleading. The documentation for `PopupMenu` states:~~\n\n> Note: The ID values used for items are limited to 32 bits, not full 64 bits of [int](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_int.html#class-int). This has a range of -2^32 to 2^32 - 1, i.e. -2147483648 to 2147483647.\n\n~~But it only actually accepts [-1, 2147483647], with -1 used as a sentinel value. I know it's only talking about what an int can hold and not the actual accepted range, but I think doing so is confusing without clarification. The actual range isn't specified anywhere I can see, although it's perhaps implied by -1 having special meaning. I think we should probably include the actual range in